{
  "id": "Compound::DB00252 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "Phenytoin is linked to Cyp2c9 through two distinct pathways, both involving Efavirenz, which is a known inducer of Cyp2c9. The first pathway involves Phenytoin directly binding to Cyp2c18, which in turn participates in the arachidonic acid monooxygenase activity, a process that Cyp2c9 is involved in. This suggests a potential indirect interaction between Phenytoin and Cyp2c9 through the Cyp2c18 enzyme. The second pathway involves Phenytoin being classified as a cytochrome P450 3a inducer, which includes Efavirenz, a compound that directly binds to Cyp2c9. This indicates that Phenytoin may influence Cyp2c9 through its ability to induce the expression or activity of the enzyme. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Phenytoin could modulate Cyp2c9, though the exact nature of this modulation remains to be fully elucidated.",
